{
  "chapter_id": "CH007",
  "title": "Loved Exactly as Jesus Is Loved",
  "sections": [
    {
      "section_id": "SEC031",
      "title": "No Condition in the Text",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "There is no bigger scripture than this: Jesus prayed that the world would know that the Father sent him, and that the Father loved believers exactly as he loved Jesus. God loves you exactly the way he loves Jesus. If you are looking for a preaching topic, you will not find a greater one than that.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA114",
            "SRC003105",
            "SRC003106",
            "SRC003107",
            "SRC003108",
            "SRC003110",
            "SRC003111",
            "REF020"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC003105",
            "SRC003106",
            "SRC003107",
            "SRC003108",
            "SRC003110",
            "SRC003111",
            "SRC002417",
            "SRC002434",
            "SRC002570",
            "SRC002590"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA114"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [
            "REF020"
          ],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000001",
          "provider_handle": "p1"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet preachers often attach conditions to that statement that are simply not in the text. They say it is true as long as you stay right, as long as you preserve yourself, as long as you put all your heart in the Lord. They put that condition there; they made that condition. But is that what he actually said? That is not what he said in the verse. The love described is not qualified by any such clause.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA115",
            "SRC003118",
            "SRC003123",
            "SRC003124",
            "SRC003125",
            "SRC003126",
            "SRC003128",
            "SRC003134",
            "SRC003135"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC003118",
            "SRC003123",
            "SRC003124",
            "SRC003125",
            "SRC003126",
            "SRC003128",
            "SRC003134",
            "SRC003135"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA115"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000002",
          "provider_handle": "p2"
        },
        {
          "text": "God knows your weakness already; your weakness is not a revelation to him. The call is to dare to believe that he loves you the same way regardless of what he already knows about you. And when you dare to believe that, you discover that the love of God is able to keep you pure. It is his goodness that brought redemption to us, not his judgment. It is his goodness, not his judgment, that produces the transformation.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA116",
            "SRC003142",
            "SRC003143",
            "SRC003144",
            "SRC003145",
            "SRC003146",
            "SRC003147",
            "SRC003148",
            "SRC003149",
            "SRC003150",
            "SRC003151",
            "SRC003152"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC003142",
            "SRC003143",
            "SRC003144",
            "SRC003145",
            "SRC003146",
            "SRC003147",
            "SRC003148",
            "SRC003149",
            "SRC003150",
            "SRC003151",
            "SRC003152"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA116"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000003",
          "provider_handle": "p3"
        }
      ],
      "idea_refs": [
        "IDEA114",
